  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cleaner Air and Better Health</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  . ..The Government of India (GOI) identified air pollution as a major challenge for public health and had initiated the National Clean Air Program (NCAP) in 2019. Using FY 2022 resources the Cleaner Air and Better Health activity will provide technical assistance to the Government of India for mitigation of air pollution by assessing the need for regulatory reforms for improving air quality governance, improving the technical understanding of sources of air pollution, such as burning of municipal solid waste (including plastic waste) that also contributes to climate change through release of short-lived climate pollutants (SLCPs) such as black carbon; developing protocols for monitoring and management of indoor air quality; and building capacity on air quality and health for clinicians and other health workers... .. .</narrative>
  </description>
